I am finishing my bachelor degree with a minor in Creative writing and starting graduate studies in Environmental education.

I live in Tiohti:áke/Montreall, in the wonderful neighborhood of Hochelaga, learning everyday about the birds who are flying around me.   
  
I work for the environmental coalition [Front commun pour la transition énergique](https://www.pourlatransitionenergetique.org/) where I  support knowledge management and learning processes of the team around the project [Collectivités ZéN](https://www.pourlatransitionenergetique.org/le-projet-collectivite-zen/). 

I also dedicated a lot of my time on my newly founded non-profit, [Fleurs d'attache](https://www.instagram.com/fleursdattache/), which aims at nurturing radical curiosity and reconnecting ecoanxious young adults to the nature in Tiohti:áke to helps us become better ecocitizens.  



